  "notes": ["Only function code 03 (read holding registers) is supported, up to 125 registers per request. Slave address 1 to 247; baud rate 4800 to 38400, 8 data bits, 1 or 2 stop bits, even, odd or no parity (set on the instrument).", "The same measurements appear in three banks: scaled 32-bit integers from 4096, IEEE 754 floats from 12288 (no scaling needed) and 16-bit values from 80/100 expressed as a fraction of the rated value (16384 = rated value). Use the float bank when possible.", "The manual does not state the word order; values are read with the most significant word first.", "Energy values are integers holding the energy x 100 (Wh x 100, varh x 100 and so on), so the map scales them by 0.01.", "In the 16-bit bank the manual marks the formats with an asterisk it does not explain; the rated values come from the CT, VT and nominal power registers 80 to 88.", "Requesting registers past the end of the map returns zeros; starting at an address that is not listed returns exception 02."],
